<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33038" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏrōdes</span></b> , is
			(<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen.</i> also
			Orodi, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 5, 18, 1</span></i> Orell. <i>N. cr.;</i>
			<i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 21, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam.
				15, 1, 2</span></i>), m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρώδης</span>, <i>a male proper name.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A king of the Parthians</i>, <i>who
				took Crassus prisoner and put him to death</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				6, 1, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 2, 46, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 3,
				11, 4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Orodes</i>, <i>son of the former</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Tac. A.
				6, 35</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A king of the Colchians</i>, <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 5,
				28</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>A king of the Albanians</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Eutr. 6, 11</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>V.</b>
			<i>The name of a warrior slain by Mezentius</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				10, 732</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
